            <ArticleTitle>Partial Deletion of Chromosome 1p31.1 Including only the Neuronal Growth Regulator 1 Gene in Two Siblings.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>23-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1055/s-0035-1554977</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present two siblings with a partial deletion of chromosome 1p31.1 involving only the neuronal growth regulator 1 (NEGR1) gene. The siblings had a history of neuropsychiatric and behavioral problems, learning difficulties, hypotonia, mild aortic root dilatation, hypermobility, and scoliosis. This is the first clinical report of a microdeletion of chromosome 1p31.1 involving only the NEGR1 gene.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
